{"id":"0d4b674ed976a9bead536d3039cb29e57bf2753e","axis":"silent","repo":"scrapy/scrapy","sha":"0d4b674ed976a9bead536d3039cb29e57bf2753e","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"conftest.py","lines":["@@ -289,6 +289,7 @@ def pytest_runtest_setup(item):","         \"botocore\",","         \"boto3\",","         \"aioboto3\",","+        \"keyring\",","         \"psutil\",","     ]"," "],"additions":1,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"docs/topics/settings.rst","lines":["@@ -239,6 +239,60 @@ The ``settings`` object can be used like a :class:`dict` (e.g."," which may be passed from the command line as strings, it is recommended to use"," one of the methods provided by the :class:`~scrapy.settings.Settings` API."," ","+.. _secret-settings:","+","+Secret settings","+===============","+","+Settings that hold credentials, such as :setting:`AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY`, can","+reference a secret stored elsewhere instead:","+","+.. code-block:: python","+","+    AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID = {\"env\": \"AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID\"}","+    AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY = {\"keyring\": \"aws\"}","+    FTP_PASSWORD = {","+        \"keyring\": {","+            \"username\": \"ftp\",","+            \"service\": \"myproject\",","+            \"backend\": \"keyring.backends.SecretService.Keyring\",","+        }","+    }","+","+``{\"env\": \"VAR\"}`` reads the ``VAR`` environment variable.","+","+``{\"keyring\": …}`` reads from a keyring_ (21.7.0 or later) entry, given either","+its username or an object with its ``username``, ``service`` (default:","+``\"scrapy\"``) and the import path of the keyring ``backend`` to use instead of","+the default one.","+","+.. _keyring: https://pypi.org/project/keyring/","+","+A missing environment variable or keyring entry raises :exc:`KeyError`.","+","+From the command line, write references as JSON:","+","+.. code-block:: shell","+","+    scrapy crawl myspider -s 'AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID={\"env\": \"AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID\"}'","+","+To set a secret that is itself a JSON object with an ``env``, ``keyring`` or","+``raw`` key, wrap it in a ``raw`` key: ``'{\"raw\": {\"env\": \"production\", …}}'``.","+","+To load environment variables from a :file:`.env` file, run Scrapy through","+`dotenv run`_ or through a secrets manager command like 1Password’s `op run`_,","+which also resolves secret references in the file:","+","+.. code-block:: shell","+","+    dotenv run -- scrapy crawl myspider","+    op run --env-file=.env -- scrapy crawl myspider","+","+.. _dotenv run: https://pypi.org/project/python-dotenv/","+.. _op run: https://developer.1password.com/docs/cli/reference/commands/run/","+","+Components read secret settings with","+:meth:`~scrapy.settings.BaseSettings.getsecret`."," "," .. _component-priority-dictionaries:"," ","@@ -473,6 +527,8 @@ Default: ``None``"," The AWS access key used by code that requires access to `Amazon Web services`_,"," such as the :ref:`S3 feed storage backend <topics-feed-storage-s3>`."," ","+This is a :ref:`secret setting <secret-settings>`.","+"," .. setting:: AWS_ENDPOINT_URL"," "," AWS_ENDPOINT_URL","@@ -521,6 +577,8 @@ Default: ``None``"," The AWS secret key used by code that requires access to `Amazon Web services`_,"," such as the :ref:`S3 feed storage backend <topics-feed-storage-s3>`."," ","+This is a :ref:`secret setting <secret-settings>`.","+"," .. setting:: AWS_SESSION_TOKEN"," "," AWS_SESSION_TOKEN","@@ -532,6 +590,8 @@ The AWS security token used by code that requires access to `Amazon Web services"," such as the :ref:`S3 feed storage backend <topics-feed-storage-s3>`, when using"," `temporary security credentials`_."," ","+This is a :ref:`secret setting <secret-settings>`.","+"," .. _temporary security credentials: https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/security-creds.html"," "," .. setting:: AWS_USE_SSL","@@ -1586,6 +1646,8 @@ Default: ``\"guest\"``"," The password to use for FTP connections when there is no ``\"ftp_password\"``"," in ``Request`` meta."," ","+This is a :ref:`secret setting <secret-settings>`.","+"," It can be overridden in a request in any of the following ways:"," "," -   Specifying ``ftp_password`` in :attr:`Request.meta <scrapy.http.Request.meta>`"],"additions":62,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"pyproject.toml","lines":["@@ -123,6 +123,7 @@ pattern = \"^(?P<version>.+)$\""," [tool.mypy]"," strict = true"," untyped_calls_exclude = [","+    \"keyring\",","     \"twisted\","," ]"," ","@@ -309,6 +310,7 @@ markers = [","     \"requires_aioboto3: marks tests that need aiobotocore and aioboto3\",","     \"requires_psutil: marks tests that need psutil\",","     \"requires_mitmproxy: marks tests that need a mitmdump executable\",","+    \"requires_keyring: marks tests that need keyring\",","     \"requires_internet: marks tests that need real Internet access\",","     \"walltime: marks benchmarks that need CodSpeed's walltime mode to be meaningful\","," ]"],"additions":2,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"scrapy/core/downloader/handlers/_aioftp.py","lines":["@@ -107,7 +107,7 @@ def __init__(self, crawler: Crawler):","                 f\"{type(self).__name__} does not support disabling FTP_PASSIVE_MODE.\"","             )","         self._user: str = crawler.settings[\"FTP_USER\"]","-        self._password: str = crawler.settings[\"FTP_PASSWORD\"]","+        self._password: str = crawler.settings.getsecret(\"FTP_PASSWORD\") or \"\"","         self._ssl_context: ssl.SSLContext = _make_ssl_context(crawler.settings)"," ","     @asynccontextmanager"],"additions":1,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"scrapy/core/downloader/handlers/ftp.py","lines":["@@ -132,7 +132,7 @@ def __init__(self, crawler: Crawler):","             raise NotConfigured(f\"{type(self).__name__} requires a Twisted reactor.\")","         super().__init__(crawler)","         self.default_user = crawler.settings[\"FTP_USER\"]","-        self.default_password = crawler.settings[\"FTP_PASSWORD\"]","+        self.default_password = crawler.settings.getsecret(\"FTP_PASSWORD\")